WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.235
Gentlemen, this is
the dreaded bone chop.

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:05.638
This thing's a beast.

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:07.273
All I ever wanted to hear.

00:00:10.843 --> 00:00:12.078
WIL WILLIS: The Yatagan.

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:17.383
The Yatagan was prominently
used by elite infantry

00:00:17.449 --> 00:00:21.120
soldiers in Ottoman Turkey from
the 16th to 19th centuries.

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:22.655
Revered for its
extreme light weight

00:00:22.755 --> 00:00:25.391
and lethal forward curve,
it was a quick and deadly

00:00:25.457 --> 00:00:29.762
slicer, while its strong tapered
tip made it powerful thrust.

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:33.032
It also featured a unique yet
practical pommel that contained

00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:34.901
flared out ears to
prevent it from slipping

00:00:35.001 --> 00:00:36.202
from the hand of battle.

00:00:36.268 --> 00:00:38.270
A fierce and respected
weapon, the Yatagan

00:00:38.337 --> 00:00:40.139
was most notably
wielded by Suleiman

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:42.008
the Magnificent,
the longest reigning

00:00:42.074 --> 00:00:43.643
sultan of the Ottoman Empire.

00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:46.012
Bladesmiths, to see
what kind of lethal damage

00:00:46.078 --> 00:00:47.713
your weapon will do,
I'll take your Yatagan

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:50.950
and deliver slashes and thrusts
on this ballistics dummy.

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:52.551
Dave, you're first.
Are you ready?

00:00:52.618 --> 00:00:53.452
Yes, sir.

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:55.188
Let's do this.

00:00:55.288 --> 00:00:56.656
I'm so nervous right now.

00:00:56.756 --> 00:01:02.095
And I'm just hoping that
my blade will perform well.

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:06.666
[music playing]

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:17.376
She's got bowels
dripping out of her.

00:01:17.477 --> 00:01:19.078
Let's talk about
your weapon, Dave.

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:21.614
It follows the feel of a
Yatagan that's supposed

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:23.616
to be light and deadly.

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:28.654
The edge you have here is sharp,
which curved in to lacerate.

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:30.890
Your Yatagan will kill.

00:01:30.957 --> 00:01:32.157
Thank you very much.

00:01:32.224 --> 00:01:33.392
All right, Gabe, your turn.

00:01:33.459 --> 00:01:34.394
You ready?

00:01:34.461 --> 00:01:36.462
Go nuts, man.

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:41.501
[music playing]

00:01:47.774 --> 00:01:50.543
All right, Gabe,
it is so light,

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:52.479
it really feels
like it's not there.

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:53.746
It's almost scary.

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:58.451
When I thrust, it penetrates
easily and slashes down.

00:01:58.518 --> 00:02:01.654
Overall, sir, your
blade will kill.

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:03.022
Thank you.

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:05.491
All right, gentlemen,
this is the strength test.

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:07.393
To test the strength
of your weapon,

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:10.829
I'll be chopping into
these bones six times.

00:02:10.896 --> 00:02:12.732
Dave, you're up first.

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:14.733
Hacking bone is
a very difficult

00:02:14.833 --> 00:02:17.036
thing to do with a thin edge.

00:02:17.103 --> 00:02:21.807
I'm aghast knowing what's
going to be coming.

00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:27.413
[music playing]

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:37.323
All right, David,
that's a tough test.

00:02:37.423 --> 00:02:39.559
Those are very thick bones.

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:42.862
But what we've got going on
here is a lot of chipping

00:02:42.928 --> 00:02:44.396
and distortion on your blade.

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:49.034
We've also got a major
crack in your handle that

00:02:49.134 --> 00:02:52.237
runs right up through the pins.

00:02:52.304 --> 00:02:53.872
All right, Gabe, your turn.

00:02:53.939 --> 00:02:54.873
You're ready for this?

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:56.609
Go nuts.

00:02:56.676 --> 00:03:01.181
[music playing]

00:03:10.155 --> 00:03:13.459
OK, Gabe, the convex
edge you've got on here

00:03:13.525 --> 00:03:17.029
is pretty much the perfect
edge for a test like this.

00:03:17.096 --> 00:03:19.799
It's sharp and strong.

00:03:19.899 --> 00:03:25.471
I can feel just the
smallest amount of a roll.

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:26.505
Nicely done.

00:03:26.572 --> 00:03:28.141
Thank you.

00:03:28.241 --> 00:03:30.243
All right, gentlemen,
next up, the sharpness test.

00:03:30.309 --> 00:03:32.678
For that, I'll give you to Doug.

00:03:32.745 --> 00:03:36.382
Bladesmiths, to see if
your blade is still sharp,

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:39.619
I will take your weapon and
slash through these silks.

00:03:39.685 --> 00:03:42.521
If your blade is still
sharp, it should cut cleanly.

00:03:42.622 --> 00:03:46.626
If not, it may rip or
tear or worse do nothing.

00:03:46.693 --> 00:03:47.993
Dave, you're up first.
You ready?

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:48.995
Yes, sir.

00:03:49.062 --> 00:03:51.163
Let's do this.

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:55.768
[music playing]

00:04:02.441 --> 00:04:06.278
All right, I love the
balance of your blade.

00:04:06.378 --> 00:04:08.114
I like the way it curves in.

00:04:08.214 --> 00:04:11.517
But you can really
feel the edges now.

00:04:11.618 --> 00:04:12.685
It's serrated.

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:14.354
It hangs up with silk.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:17.222
But then on the last piece,
just when it's nice and taut,

00:04:17.289 --> 00:04:19.558
it can lacerate
and cut through it.

00:04:19.658 --> 00:04:22.528
Overall, your blade
will still cut.

00:04:22.628 --> 00:04:23.362
Thank you.

00:04:23.462 --> 00:04:24.731
All right, Gabe,
it's your turn.

00:04:24.831 --> 00:04:26.165
You ready?
- I'm ready.

00:04:26.232 --> 00:04:28.234
Let's do this.

00:04:28.301 --> 00:04:33.473
[music playing]

00:04:44.416 --> 00:04:48.087
All right, Gabe, your
blade is so light,

00:04:48.187 --> 00:04:50.289
you're barely
cutting through air.

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:53.225
I glided through
this, lacerated,

00:04:53.325 --> 00:04:55.528
and of course, in the
finishing cuts here,

00:04:55.594 --> 00:04:58.464
cut easily through that silk.

00:04:58.531 --> 00:04:59.699
It cuts.

00:04:59.799 --> 00:05:00.700
Good job.

00:05:00.767 --> 00:05:02.935
Thank you very much.

00:05:03.035 --> 00:05:06.706
Bladesmiths, you both created
remarkable finale weapons.

00:05:06.773 --> 00:05:08.507
But in this arena
of competition,

00:05:08.574 --> 00:05:11.277
there can only be one
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:05:11.344 --> 00:05:17.016
And that champion is Gabe.

00:05:17.083 --> 00:05:21.020
Congratulations, you are the
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:05:21.087 --> 00:05:24.256
Dave, please
surrender your weapon.

00:05:24.323 --> 00:05:26.325
DAVE: It's exactly
what I expected.

00:05:26.391 --> 00:05:27.993
It was very difficult
testing, but I'm

00:05:28.093 --> 00:05:32.064
still the guy with the cracked
edge and the broken handle.

00:05:32.164 --> 00:05:33.332
Gabe, congratulations.

00:05:33.432 --> 00:05:34.800
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:37.703
and will be receiving
a check for $10,000.

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:39.005
Good job.

00:05:39.105 --> 00:05:40.372
I've never seen
anybody less stoked

00:05:40.472 --> 00:05:42.908
about getting $10,000
in my entire life.

00:05:42.975 --> 00:05:45.777
Why don't you please present
that weapon to the judges?

00:05:45.878 --> 00:05:47.913
It feels great to be the
"Forged in Fire" champion,

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:50.683
but I'll do my celebrating
behind closed doors.

00:05:50.783 --> 00:05:53.819
I felt like I was the
underdog, but underdogs

00:05:53.919 --> 00:05:56.322
win sometimes I guess.

00:05:56.389 --> 00:06:01.594
[music playing]

00:06:05.264 --> 00:06:07.232
Holy [bleep].

00:06:07.299 --> 00:06:10.770
WIL WILLIS: The Indian
two handed sword.

00:06:10.836 --> 00:06:13.606
Emerging around the 17th
century, this rare two handed

00:06:13.672 --> 00:06:16.642
sword joins some of the most
iconic bladed weapons produced

00:06:16.742 --> 00:06:18.177
in the Indian subcontinent.

00:06:18.277 --> 00:06:21.113
The long double edged blade
reached lengths of up to five

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:22.948
feet, and was so
heavy, it required

00:06:23.015 --> 00:06:26.652
the wielder to use two hands
for more accurate strikes.

00:06:26.752 --> 00:06:29.622
It also featured three brass
globes positioned on the shaft

00:06:29.688 --> 00:06:32.925
that offered a more secure grip
as well as a counterbalance

00:06:32.992 --> 00:06:34.527
for the heavy blade.

00:06:34.594 --> 00:06:37.930
Despite its substantial size,
the blade was designed to flex.

00:06:37.996 --> 00:06:41.267
By the mid-18th century,
improved gunpowder technology

00:06:41.334 --> 00:06:43.836
spread throughout India,
making the Indian two

00:06:43.903 --> 00:06:46.472
handed sword obsolete.

00:06:46.538 --> 00:06:48.841
Bladesmiths, this
is the kill test.

00:06:48.908 --> 00:06:51.476
To see what kind of lethal
damage your weapon will do,

00:06:51.576 --> 00:06:53.279
we'll take your sword
and deliver killing

00:06:53.379 --> 00:06:55.047
blows on this boar carcass.

00:06:55.114 --> 00:06:56.181
Jonathan, you're up first.

00:06:56.248 --> 00:06:57.182
You ready?

00:06:57.249 --> 00:06:58.918
Go for it.

00:06:58.985 --> 00:07:03.956
[music playing]

00:07:15.935 --> 00:07:18.003
All right, Jonathan, let's
talk about your sword right

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:19.004
here.

00:07:19.071 --> 00:07:21.406
First up, it's sharp.

00:07:21.473 --> 00:07:23.775
Definitely lacerated
through easily.

00:07:23.842 --> 00:07:26.846
When wielding this weapon,
there's a nice balance to it.

00:07:26.912 --> 00:07:30.416
Overall, your weapon,
sir, will kill.

00:07:30.483 --> 00:07:31.416
Thank you.

00:07:31.516 --> 00:07:33.586
Ed, are you ready?

00:07:33.686 --> 00:07:36.121
I am.

00:07:36.222 --> 00:07:40.726
[music playing]

00:07:49.335 --> 00:07:51.770
All right, Ed, let's talk
about your weapon right here.

00:07:51.837 --> 00:07:54.440
First up, I like the
leather wrapping that you

00:07:54.506 --> 00:07:55.440
did right here on the handle.

00:07:55.507 --> 00:07:57.009
It gives it a good grip.

00:07:57.076 --> 00:07:59.545
Your blade is a little
bit on the heavier side.

00:07:59.611 --> 00:08:05.918
But upon the swing, it lacerates
deeply into the carcass.

00:08:05.985 --> 00:08:07.019
It will kill.

00:08:10.022 --> 00:08:12.425
Gentlemen, this is
the dreaded bone chop.

00:08:12.525 --> 00:08:13.659
Remember, this test
is all about what

00:08:13.759 --> 00:08:15.260
the bones do to your
blades and not what

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:17.096
your blades do to the bones.

00:08:17.163 --> 00:08:18.029
Ed, you're up first.

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:19.064
Are you ready?

00:08:19.131 --> 00:08:20.899
Mm-hmm.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:26.506
[music playing]

00:08:30.910 --> 00:08:33.579
Well, Ed, it's
all in one piece,

00:08:33.679 --> 00:08:36.782
but there is some chipping
on the blade here.

00:08:36.882 --> 00:08:38.150
Oh, shoot.

00:08:38.217 --> 00:08:40.219
The sword itself is heavy.

00:08:40.286 --> 00:08:42.488
The handle is a bit
big for my hand.

00:08:42.588 --> 00:08:45.357
All that being said, it
held up relatively well.

00:08:45.424 --> 00:08:46.926
Well done.
- Thank you.

00:08:46.993 --> 00:08:47.893
Jonathan, you're up.

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:48.894
Are you ready?

00:08:48.961 --> 00:08:51.163
Hope so.

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:56.202
[music playing]

00:09:03.942 --> 00:09:05.844
Well, Jonathan,
it's a similar result.

00:09:05.944 --> 00:09:08.914
There is some edge
chipping here as well.

00:09:09.014 --> 00:09:13.786
The handle being round on one
of the hits did roll in my hand.

00:09:13.886 --> 00:09:17.490
Aside from edge chipping,
held up very well.

00:09:17.590 --> 00:09:18.491
Well done.

00:09:18.591 --> 00:09:19.792
Thank you.

00:09:21.460 --> 00:09:23.629
All right, gentlemen, to test
the sharpness of your blade,

00:09:23.695 --> 00:09:25.163
I'll be cutting
through these pumpkins.

00:09:25.263 --> 00:09:27.667
We'll take a look at those cuts
and see how clean they are.

00:09:27.767 --> 00:09:28.868
Jonathan, you're up.

00:09:28.935 --> 00:09:29.868
Are you ready?

00:09:29.935 --> 00:09:32.237
I'm ready.

00:09:32.338 --> 00:09:37.310
[music playing]

00:09:48.286 --> 00:09:52.525
So Jonathan, you can see, your
blade has such a flexibility

00:09:52.592 --> 00:09:56.095
to it that when it hit,
the blade actually warped

00:09:56.162 --> 00:09:58.397
that cut over and through.

00:09:58.497 --> 00:09:59.865
It's a heck of a cutter.

00:09:59.932 --> 00:10:00.899
Nicely done.

00:10:00.966 --> 00:10:02.601
Thank you.

00:10:02.701 --> 00:10:04.269
All right, Ed, you're up.

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:06.238
Are you ready?

00:10:06.305 --> 00:10:11.243
[music playing]

00:10:14.346 --> 00:10:17.816
All right, Ed, that's a good,
clean cut on that pumpkin.

00:10:17.883 --> 00:10:19.785
You can kind of
see what happened.

00:10:19.885 --> 00:10:21.653
I started compensating
for the weight

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:23.556
and pulled up and through.

00:10:23.656 --> 00:10:26.959
The weight factor in me
using it is an issue.

00:10:27.026 --> 00:10:30.195
But definitely sharp,
definitely a good cutter.

00:10:30.262 --> 00:10:31.664
Well done.

00:10:31.731 --> 00:10:33.766
It's really hard to say one
way or the other right now

00:10:33.832 --> 00:10:36.101
who could and couldn't
win this thing.

00:10:36.201 --> 00:10:39.137
Jonathan, Ed, the judges have
finished their deliberation,

00:10:39.237 --> 00:10:41.640
and there can only be one
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:47.747
And that champion is Jonathan.

00:10:47.813 --> 00:10:50.983
Congratulations, you are our
new "Forged in Fire" champion.

00:10:51.083 --> 00:10:53.852
Ed, your sword
didn't make the cut.

00:10:53.919 --> 00:10:56.688
Please surrender your blade.

00:10:56.755 --> 00:10:58.423
ED: I agree with the
judges' decision.

00:10:58.490 --> 00:10:59.958
His blade was more usable.

00:11:00.025 --> 00:11:02.694
I made a good blade, he made
a little bit better blade.

00:11:02.761 --> 00:11:07.366
No matter what, I'm
still a happy cat.

00:11:07.466 --> 00:11:09.201
Jonathan, good job.

00:11:09.268 --> 00:11:12.070
You are our new "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:11:12.137 --> 00:11:14.139
And that's a title that comes
with a check for how much

00:11:14.206 --> 00:11:15.507
money?
- $10,000.

00:11:15.574 --> 00:11:16.942
$10,000, that's right.

00:11:17.042 --> 00:11:18.109
Thank you.

00:11:18.210 --> 00:11:20.579
Jonathan, please present
your blade to the judges.

00:11:20.680 --> 00:11:22.848
I won "Forged in Fire"
and that's pretty awesome.

00:11:22.915 --> 00:11:24.817
It's not really sunk
in yet that I won.

00:11:24.917 --> 00:11:26.051
I'd love to have one
of those grinders,

00:11:26.118 --> 00:11:29.588
so I might buy some
shop tools too.

00:11:29.655 --> 00:11:32.090
We'll see.

00:11:32.191 --> 00:11:37.229
[music playing]

00:11:39.198 --> 00:11:40.899
J. Nielson's war scythe.

00:11:40.999 --> 00:11:44.269
This war scythe was
personally created by our very

00:11:44.336 --> 00:11:46.906
own beast from the East.

00:11:47.006 --> 00:11:49.208
This war scythe is
a menacing variation

00:11:49.274 --> 00:11:52.645
on a centuries old peasant's
weapon from Middle Age Europe.

00:11:52.745 --> 00:11:54.213
Ready for battle at
a moment's notice,

00:11:54.313 --> 00:11:56.949
farmers would take their
scythes from work to war

00:11:57.015 --> 00:11:59.851
during uprisings, riots,
or calls to battle.

00:11:59.918 --> 00:12:02.921
This weapon uses a long shaft
to generate massive power

00:12:02.988 --> 00:12:05.824
to cut down enemies, while
its lethal sharp point

00:12:05.890 --> 00:12:08.160
could be thrust into
infantry and cavalry.

00:12:08.260 --> 00:12:10.896
This multifaceted
scythe features a fork

00:12:10.996 --> 00:12:13.832
opposite the blade
as a piercing element

00:12:13.898 --> 00:12:15.767
and a small blade at
the bottom of the pole

00:12:15.834 --> 00:12:17.536
to finish off an opponent.

00:12:17.602 --> 00:12:19.672
Scythes are represented
in pop culture

00:12:19.739 --> 00:12:22.307
as sinister and ominous
weapons symbolizing death,

00:12:22.374 --> 00:12:25.911
and is most notoriously
wielded by the grim reaper.

00:12:25.978 --> 00:12:30.883
Up first, our very
own dealer of death,

00:12:30.950 --> 00:12:34.653
the doer of deadly
deeds, the kill

00:12:34.753 --> 00:12:40.692
test master, Doug Marcaida.

00:12:40.792 --> 00:12:43.195
Yeah, he just looks
like a murderer.

00:12:43.295 --> 00:12:46.431
I am really nervous.

00:12:46.532 --> 00:12:51.036
[music playing]

00:13:13.592 --> 00:13:16.529
All right, Alex,
the balance is light,

00:13:16.595 --> 00:13:18.030
allowing it to be
a very fast weapon

00:13:18.130 --> 00:13:21.934
that you can use either for long
handed or for close quarters.

00:13:22.034 --> 00:13:24.403
Your weapon will kill.

00:13:27.072 --> 00:13:28.707
All right, Trevor,
trick or treat?

00:13:28.774 --> 00:13:29.708
Treat?

00:13:29.775 --> 00:13:32.210
Indeed.

00:13:32.311 --> 00:13:37.817
[music playing]

00:14:02.574 --> 00:14:07.145
All right, Trevor, the tip alone
penetrates deeply into the gut,

00:14:07.212 --> 00:14:09.047
and the edges here
are sharp enough to,

00:14:09.114 --> 00:14:10.915
well, make it lose its head.

00:14:10.982 --> 00:14:13.118
Overall, sir, it will kill.

00:14:13.219 --> 00:14:14.220
Thank you, sir.

00:14:18.991 --> 00:14:21.627
All right, smiths, welcome
to the strength test,

00:14:21.693 --> 00:14:24.930
the dreaded coffin challenge.

00:14:24.996 --> 00:14:27.566
I'm going to take these bones
and beat them repeatedly

00:14:27.632 --> 00:14:29.201
into the blade of your scythes.

00:14:29.268 --> 00:14:31.770
And Alex, you're locked
in and ready to go first.

00:14:31.837 --> 00:14:32.972
You ready?

00:14:33.072 --> 00:14:33.805
Yep.

00:14:33.872 --> 00:14:37.376
That's what I want to hear.

00:14:37.443 --> 00:14:42.414
[music playing]

00:14:59.565 --> 00:15:00.532
Alex, you survived.

00:15:00.599 --> 00:15:01.866
Good job.

00:15:01.967 --> 00:15:03.268
The only issue I have, you
have some slight rolling

00:15:03.368 --> 00:15:04.636
on the edge.

00:15:04.703 --> 00:15:07.906
And the head of this moves,
so it's not secure anymore.

00:15:08.006 --> 00:15:09.341
But your edge held up great.

00:15:09.408 --> 00:15:10.342
Good job.

00:15:10.409 --> 00:15:11.710
Thank you.

00:15:11.810 --> 00:15:13.011
How you feeling, Trevor?

00:15:13.078 --> 00:15:14.212
Pretty good right now.

00:15:14.279 --> 00:15:15.247
Good.

00:15:15.313 --> 00:15:17.715
We'll see how you
feel in a minute.

00:15:17.816 --> 00:15:22.922
[music playing]

00:15:34.899 --> 00:15:35.867
Nice job, Trevor.

00:15:35.968 --> 00:15:37.135
Held up well.

00:15:37.202 --> 00:15:39.504
Your edge is still
good, nice and sharp.

00:15:39.571 --> 00:15:41.206
Everything's still tight.

00:15:41.306 --> 00:15:42.440
Good job.

00:15:42.507 --> 00:15:43.542
Thank you.

00:15:47.412 --> 00:15:49.848
All right, bladesmiths,
this is the sharpness

00:15:49.915 --> 00:15:51.951
test, the zombie surprise.

00:15:54.820 --> 00:15:57.622
To test the edge of your weapon,
I'm going to take your scythe

00:15:57.689 --> 00:16:01.593
and cut through this rope,
thereby releasing a surprise.

00:16:01.660 --> 00:16:02.627
All right.

00:16:02.727 --> 00:16:03.662
Alex, you're up first.

00:16:03.729 --> 00:16:04.729
You ready?

00:16:04.796 --> 00:16:07.599
Certainly.

00:16:07.666 --> 00:16:12.237
[music playing]

00:16:35.293 --> 00:16:38.129
All right, Alex, it
cut easily on the rope.

00:16:38.196 --> 00:16:42.901
When you're puncturing this,
it cuts through and slices.

00:16:42.968 --> 00:16:44.636
It'll cut.

00:16:44.703 --> 00:16:45.871
Thank you.

00:16:45.938 --> 00:16:47.239
All right, Trevor,
your turn, sir.

00:16:47.306 --> 00:16:48.240
You ready?

00:16:48.307 --> 00:16:50.709
Hell yeah.

00:16:50.776 --> 00:16:55.347
[music playing]

00:17:26.611 --> 00:17:29.948
All right, Trevor, the edge
that you have here lends itself

00:17:30.048 --> 00:17:31.750
to cut the rope much easier.

00:17:31.817 --> 00:17:33.318
When you're
puncturing, it starts

00:17:33.418 --> 00:17:34.920
to cut all the way through.

00:17:35.020 --> 00:17:36.554
Overall, sir, it will cut.

00:17:36.621 --> 00:17:37.589
Thank you.

00:17:40.758 --> 00:17:43.261
All right, bladesmiths, you
guys have done fantastic work,

00:17:43.328 --> 00:17:45.931
but only one of you can be
the "Forged in Fire" champion,

00:17:46.031 --> 00:17:51.202
and that champion is Trevor.

00:17:51.302 --> 00:17:54.572
Congratulations, you are the
new "Forged in Fire" champion.

00:17:54.673 --> 00:17:57.642
Alex, unfortunately, your
blade took some damage

00:17:57.709 --> 00:17:59.043
in our strength test.

00:17:59.144 --> 00:18:00.913
You did great work, my
friend, but at this time,

00:18:00.979 --> 00:18:04.248
I have to ask you to
please exit the forge.

00:18:04.315 --> 00:18:06.485
Ultimately, it came
down to the construction.

00:18:06.552 --> 00:18:08.019
I think I definitely
made a blade

00:18:08.086 --> 00:18:09.621
that can intimidate anyone.

00:18:12.491 --> 00:18:14.193
Well, Trevor, the
judges all agree

00:18:14.259 --> 00:18:16.428
you made a damn near perfect
war scythe which has earned you

00:18:16.528 --> 00:18:18.196
the title of "Forged
in Fire" champion

00:18:18.263 --> 00:18:19.998
and a check for $10,000.

00:18:20.064 --> 00:18:21.166
Good job, brother.

00:18:21.266 --> 00:18:23.534
Come on forward and
shake our hands.

00:18:23.601 --> 00:18:25.370
I won!

00:18:25.437 --> 00:18:26.704
Woo!

00:18:26.804 --> 00:18:28.640
I think the biggest thing I
learned was to keep on trying.

00:18:28.740 --> 00:18:31.743
If something doesn't go your
way, don't get upset about it.

00:18:31.810 --> 00:18:33.879
Just keep moving forward.

00:18:33.979 --> 00:18:35.647
This was a perfect
Halloween experience.

00:18:35.714 --> 00:18:37.148
I feel like I just
went trick or treating

00:18:37.248 --> 00:18:41.386
and I got a pillowcase
full of candy.

00:18:41.487 --> 00:18:45.524
[music playing]

00:18:50.395 --> 00:18:52.531
WIL WILLIS: Blackbeard's
infamous cutlass.

00:18:57.435 --> 00:19:00.005
Among the most notorious
pirates of the 18th century,

00:19:00.072 --> 00:19:02.341
Blackbeard terrorized
Caribbean and Atlantic

00:19:02.407 --> 00:19:04.776
merchant shipping with his
trademark cutlass in hand.

00:19:04.842 --> 00:19:07.612
Its short but thick curved blade
featured a razor sharp edge

00:19:07.679 --> 00:19:10.248
that was ideal for hacking and
splashing during close quarters

00:19:10.315 --> 00:19:12.251
combat while seizing
small vessels.

00:19:12.317 --> 00:19:16.254
In his legendary battle with
Captain Robert Maynard in 1718,

00:19:16.320 --> 00:19:17.955
Blackbeard's cutlass
broke Maynard's sword

00:19:18.022 --> 00:19:20.191
in half with a single blow.

00:19:20.292 --> 00:19:22.494
Today, Blackbeard's
menacing presence and expert

00:19:22.561 --> 00:19:25.230
swordsmanship can still
be seen in the video game

00:19:25.330 --> 00:19:26.731
"Assassin's Creed 4--

00:19:26.831 --> 00:19:28.366
Black Flag."

00:19:28.433 --> 00:19:31.135
Bladesmiths, to test the
lethality of your cutlass,

00:19:31.202 --> 00:19:32.671
I'm going to inflict
lethal wounds

00:19:32.771 --> 00:19:34.472
on these ballistic dummies.

00:19:34.573 --> 00:19:36.274
Jason, you're up first.
You ready?

00:19:36.341 --> 00:19:37.542
I sure hope so, Doug.

00:19:37.609 --> 00:19:39.710
Let's do this.

00:19:39.811 --> 00:19:44.449
[music playing]

00:20:04.636 --> 00:20:07.339
All right, Jason, you've
got a very big handle here.

00:20:07.406 --> 00:20:09.207
But at least it's
got the swells.

00:20:09.274 --> 00:20:11.209
It's got an indexing for
where I hold on to it.

00:20:11.309 --> 00:20:12.811
I can tell where the edge is.

00:20:12.878 --> 00:20:16.081
The weight that you have in this
weapon is so light in the sense

00:20:16.181 --> 00:20:18.383
that I can wield it,
even around here.

00:20:18.483 --> 00:20:20.618
You've got the
clavicle, into the ribs,

00:20:20.685 --> 00:20:26.458
all the way through the lungs,
and definitely, it will kill.

00:20:26.525 --> 00:20:28.025
All I ever wanted to hear.

00:20:28.092 --> 00:20:29.094
Made my day.

00:20:29.194 --> 00:20:30.462
Seth, you're up next.

00:20:30.529 --> 00:20:31.263
You ready?

00:20:31.330 --> 00:20:33.999
Let's get some.

00:20:34.066 --> 00:20:38.637
[music playing]

00:21:05.797 --> 00:21:09.234
All right, Seth, your sword is
forward heavy without a balance

00:21:09.334 --> 00:21:10.702
coming back.

00:21:10.769 --> 00:21:12.137
I don't know whose shoulder
it's going to hurt more,

00:21:12.204 --> 00:21:13.538
the dummy's or mine.

00:21:13.638 --> 00:21:16.508
But your weapon, sir, will kill.

00:21:16.575 --> 00:21:17.542
Thank you.

00:21:20.412 --> 00:21:23.381
To test the strength and
durability of your swords,

00:21:23.448 --> 00:21:25.250
I'll be chopping
through these bones

00:21:25.316 --> 00:21:26.952
and then attacking that peg leg.

00:21:27.018 --> 00:21:30.221
Now remember, this test is
not about what your blades

00:21:30.288 --> 00:21:31.656
do to these targets.

00:21:31.757 --> 00:21:34.092
It's about what these
targets do to your blades.

00:21:34.159 --> 00:21:35.760
Jason, you're up.
Are you ready?

00:21:35.827 --> 00:21:36.828
No.

00:21:39.064 --> 00:21:43.669
[music playing]

00:22:05.623 --> 00:22:08.559
The balance of your
weapon is really nice,

00:22:08.626 --> 00:22:10.462
which is surprising
because you've

00:22:10.562 --> 00:22:12.964
made a two handed cutlass.

00:22:13.064 --> 00:22:17.069
Your blade held up very well,
except for the one little chip.

00:22:17.169 --> 00:22:18.903
And it's not even a
chip, it's a roll.

00:22:18.970 --> 00:22:20.238
So it didn't blow out.

00:22:20.305 --> 00:22:21.606
It's a good job.

00:22:21.707 --> 00:22:22.607
Thank you, Dave.

00:22:22.674 --> 00:22:24.009
All right, Seth,
are you ready?

00:22:24.109 --> 00:22:26.143
Yes, sir.

00:22:26.244 --> 00:22:30.816
[music playing]

00:22:47.899 --> 00:22:52.471
All right, Seth, first
up, this thing's a beast.

00:22:52.571 --> 00:22:57.042
It is probably a pound heavier
than your competitor's sword.

00:22:57.142 --> 00:23:00.545
Your blade, I mean, I can
run my fingernail down this,

00:23:00.645 --> 00:23:03.415
and I can see a couple
of glinting spots,

00:23:03.515 --> 00:23:04.916
but it really didn't
take any damage.

00:23:08.186 --> 00:23:09.955
All right,
bladesmiths, let's find

00:23:10.021 --> 00:23:11.489
out if there's any edge left.

00:23:11.555 --> 00:23:14.525
This is the rope cut
and pirate sail slash.

00:23:14.592 --> 00:23:16.027
To test the edge
of your cutlass,

00:23:16.128 --> 00:23:18.697
I will cut this rope,
which will raise the sail,

00:23:18.763 --> 00:23:21.266
and then I will slash the sail.

00:23:21.333 --> 00:23:23.635
This is all about
what your sword

00:23:23.701 --> 00:23:26.070
will do to the sail and rope.

00:23:26.170 --> 00:23:27.071
Jason, you're up first.

00:23:27.171 --> 00:23:28.106
Ready?

00:23:28.173 --> 00:23:30.207
Yes, sir.

00:23:30.308 --> 00:23:35.414
[music playing]

00:23:46.824 --> 00:23:50.595
All righty, Jason, your edge
cut through the rope easily

00:23:50.662 --> 00:23:53.264
and cuts with every
part that the edge

00:23:53.331 --> 00:23:55.767
met on this pirate sail.

00:23:55.834 --> 00:23:59.670
Overall, sir, your
sword will cut.

00:23:59.737 --> 00:24:00.438
Awesome.

00:24:00.538 --> 00:24:01.806
Seth, how are you feeling?

00:24:01.873 --> 00:24:02.807
Feeling good.

00:24:02.874 --> 00:24:03.808
Let's go.

00:24:03.875 --> 00:24:05.744
Let's do this.

00:24:05.811 --> 00:24:10.215
[music playing]

00:24:29.867 --> 00:24:31.736
All right, Seth,
what are the chances

00:24:31.836 --> 00:24:34.839
you find a very dull spot on
the first cut on the rope?

00:24:34.905 --> 00:24:38.310
But on the second cut, it found
another spot that was sharp.

00:24:38.410 --> 00:24:42.012
But on the sail, working
a heavy sword like this

00:24:42.113 --> 00:24:43.114
affects my cuts.

00:24:47.219 --> 00:24:50.688
Jason, Seth, the judges
have tested your weapons,

00:24:50.755 --> 00:24:52.657
and they've made
a final decision.

00:24:52.757 --> 00:24:59.564
Our new "Forged in
Fire" champion is Jason.

00:24:59.664 --> 00:25:02.767
Congratulations, you're the
new "Forged in Fire" champion.

00:25:02.867 --> 00:25:05.770
Seth, unfortunately, your
blade did not make the cut.

00:25:05.870 --> 00:25:08.839
Please surrender your blade.

00:25:08.906 --> 00:25:11.709
Jason, congratulations, you
are our new "Forged in Fire"

00:25:11.809 --> 00:25:13.144
champion, and
that's a title that

00:25:13.244 --> 00:25:16.514
comes with a bundle of
bullion that's worth $10,000.

00:25:16.614 --> 00:25:18.415
How are you feeling right now?

00:25:18.516 --> 00:25:21.653
I mean, come on,
that's incredible.

00:25:21.753 --> 00:25:24.556
"Forged in Fire" champion?

00:25:24.623 --> 00:25:29.160
[music playing]

00:25:35.033 --> 00:25:36.535
The executioner's sword.

00:25:39.070 --> 00:25:41.539
The executioner's sword
performed its bloody work

00:25:41.639 --> 00:25:43.541
in 16th century Central Europe.

00:25:43.608 --> 00:25:45.910
Unlike combat swords,
this lethal blade

00:25:46.010 --> 00:25:49.614
features a straight double edged
cutting blade with a blunt tip,

00:25:49.681 --> 00:25:52.317
perfect for swiftly chopping
off the heads of criminals.

00:25:52.417 --> 00:25:55.853
This deadly weapon was used on
many aristocratic felons rather

00:25:55.953 --> 00:25:57.755
than the ax, since
it allowed the victim

00:25:57.822 --> 00:26:00.157
to meet his end in a
dignified kneeling position

00:26:00.224 --> 00:26:02.627
rather than laying face down
with his head on the block.

00:26:02.727 --> 00:26:04.795
While the executioner's
sword fell out of use

00:26:04.862 --> 00:26:07.031
in the early 18th century,
this gruesome sword

00:26:07.098 --> 00:26:10.702
is still wielded in the
2019 video game "Mordhau."

00:26:10.802 --> 00:26:15.739
Bladesmiths, welcome
to the kill test.

00:26:15.840 --> 00:26:18.042
The executioner's
sword, that word

00:26:18.142 --> 00:26:21.146
alone just gives you visions
of decapitated heads.

00:26:21.212 --> 00:26:23.047
So to find out what
kind of lethal damage

00:26:23.114 --> 00:26:28.553
your executioner's sword can do,
I'll deliver some lethal blows

00:26:28.620 --> 00:26:31.255
on this ballistics dummy.

00:26:31.322 --> 00:26:32.257
Nathan, is it time?

00:26:32.357 --> 00:26:33.258
It's time.

00:26:33.358 --> 00:26:35.993
Have fun.

00:26:36.094 --> 00:26:40.665
[music playing]

00:26:46.437 --> 00:26:48.439
Holy crap.

00:26:48.506 --> 00:26:49.975
Just a little off the top.

00:26:53.278 --> 00:26:56.981
All right, Nathan, first
up, this is a heavy beast.

00:26:57.081 --> 00:27:01.019
It is so forward heavy that you
need two hands to control that.

00:27:01.085 --> 00:27:03.621
Now your handle
construction is smooth.

00:27:03.688 --> 00:27:04.989
I'll give you that.

00:27:05.090 --> 00:27:07.525
But it also feels a little
bit rounded over here,

00:27:07.591 --> 00:27:10.261
where it actually gives
me much more control

00:27:10.327 --> 00:27:12.763
sideways than it does this way.

00:27:12.830 --> 00:27:17.067
But overall, your weapon,
sir, it will kill.

00:27:17.134 --> 00:27:18.436
Awesome.

00:27:18.503 --> 00:27:19.604
All right, Gunnar,
your turn, sir.

00:27:19.704 --> 00:27:21.472
Are you ready?
- Absolutely.

00:27:21.539 --> 00:27:24.008
Let's do this.

00:27:24.075 --> 00:27:28.413
[music playing]

00:27:39.924 --> 00:27:42.326
All right, Gunnar, let's
talk about your executioner's

00:27:42.427 --> 00:27:43.828
sword over here.

00:27:43.928 --> 00:27:47.631
Your blade right here
has a finer grind,

00:27:47.698 --> 00:27:49.400
so it makes it a
little bit lighter.

00:27:49.500 --> 00:27:52.770
And the edge that you have here,
when it came to that skull,

00:27:52.837 --> 00:27:55.006
just glided into that.

00:27:55.106 --> 00:27:58.476
Overall, sir, your executioner's
sword, it will kill.

00:27:58.576 --> 00:27:59.778
Thank you.

00:28:03.782 --> 00:28:05.616
All right, gentlemen, it's
time for the strength test,

00:28:05.716 --> 00:28:07.619
the skull and bone chop.

00:28:07.686 --> 00:28:09.920
To test the overall
construction of your blades

00:28:10.021 --> 00:28:11.855
as well as how they feel
while they're being used,

00:28:11.956 --> 00:28:13.757
I'll be chopping
into these skulls

00:28:13.824 --> 00:28:15.859
and that nasty giraffe bone.

00:28:15.960 --> 00:28:17.461
Nathan, you're up.
Are you ready?

00:28:17.528 --> 00:28:18.462
Yes, sir.

00:28:18.529 --> 00:28:19.964
Have fun.

00:28:20.065 --> 00:28:24.703
[music playing]

00:28:37.482 --> 00:28:38.717
Holy giraffe.

00:28:41.218 --> 00:28:43.921
All right, Nathan, so right
off, man, this thing is heavy.

00:28:43.988 --> 00:28:46.257
Once you get it moving, it's
going, but controlling it's

00:28:46.357 --> 00:28:47.659
tough.

00:28:47.726 --> 00:28:49.994
Having said that, your
edge held up beautifully.

00:28:50.061 --> 00:28:52.529
It's still just as
sharp as when I started,

00:28:52.596 --> 00:28:54.198
which is pretty darn sharp.

00:28:54.265 --> 00:28:55.532
So good job on that.

00:28:55.599 --> 00:28:57.568
Thanks, I like sharp things.

00:28:57.635 --> 00:28:59.370
Gunnar, ready?

00:28:59.436 --> 00:29:01.139
What if I said no?

00:29:01.239 --> 00:29:04.141
I'd say [laughs] you don't
watch the show much do you?

00:29:04.241 --> 00:29:06.543
Exactly.

00:29:06.644 --> 00:29:11.750
[music playing]

00:29:33.171 --> 00:29:34.538
All right, sir
Gunnar, right off,

00:29:34.639 --> 00:29:36.106
lighter blade,
easier to control.

00:29:36.206 --> 00:29:38.009
A lot of that has to do with
the fact that you've got more

00:29:38.109 --> 00:29:39.276
handle here.

00:29:39.376 --> 00:29:42.780
Now your blade, it's got
some compacting on the edges,

00:29:42.847 --> 00:29:45.249
but I wouldn't run my
finger down this edge.

00:29:45.349 --> 00:29:46.583
It's still bloody sharp.

00:29:46.650 --> 00:29:47.618
Nicely done.

00:29:47.685 --> 00:29:48.920
Thank you, sir.

00:29:52.890 --> 00:29:54.325
All right,
bladesmiths, this is

00:29:54.391 --> 00:29:58.095
the sharpness test, the
jackfruit and water jug slice.

00:29:58.195 --> 00:29:59.530
Nathan, you're up first.
Are you ready?

00:29:59.596 --> 00:30:00.698
Yes, sir.
Have fun.

00:30:00.765 --> 00:30:03.568
All right, let's do this.

00:30:03.635 --> 00:30:08.173
[music playing]

00:30:15.813 --> 00:30:18.716
Still sharp.

00:30:18.817 --> 00:30:21.919
All right, Nathan, as
far as the downward chop,

00:30:21.986 --> 00:30:24.055
it's a very clean cut.

00:30:24.121 --> 00:30:26.257
Easy, no resistance whatsoever.

00:30:26.357 --> 00:30:28.225
Now, when I was
cutting, as soon as I

00:30:28.292 --> 00:30:33.163
met the resistance of the water,
it kind of rolled on my hand.

00:30:33.263 --> 00:30:36.500
But anything that it
did have contact with,

00:30:36.567 --> 00:30:37.769
it was able to cut.

00:30:37.869 --> 00:30:40.604
Overall, sir, your
weapon, it will cut.

00:30:40.671 --> 00:30:41.872
Thank you.

00:30:41.973 --> 00:30:43.107
All right, Gunnar,
your turn, sir.

00:30:43.174 --> 00:30:44.675
You ready?
- Yes, sir, I am.

00:30:44.742 --> 00:30:46.777
Let's do this.

00:30:46.878 --> 00:30:50.982
[music playing]

00:31:03.394 --> 00:31:05.263
All right, Gunnar,
the handle construction

00:31:05.329 --> 00:31:08.032
you have here is
wide and ovoid enough

00:31:08.132 --> 00:31:09.500
to wear when I hold
on to it, I can

00:31:09.566 --> 00:31:10.901
really tell where the edge is.

00:31:10.968 --> 00:31:14.004
It's much easier to
control a blade like this.

00:31:14.071 --> 00:31:17.041
In the slice, you can
see that it cuts nicely.

00:31:17.108 --> 00:31:19.677
Overall, sir, your
weapon, it will cut.

00:31:19.777 --> 00:31:20.979
Thank you.

00:31:23.815 --> 00:31:25.750
Bladesmiths, only one
of you can leave here

00:31:25.817 --> 00:31:27.452
with the title of
"Forged in Fire" champion

00:31:27.518 --> 00:31:29.320
and get that check for $10,000.

00:31:29.420 --> 00:31:31.189
Now the judges
discussed your blades

00:31:31.255 --> 00:31:33.891
and they made a final decision.

00:31:33.958 --> 00:31:35.426
Today's "Forged
in Fire" champion

00:31:35.493 --> 00:31:41.098
is Gunnar, congratulations.

00:31:41.198 --> 00:31:43.067
Now Nathan, you fought
hard man, but unfortunately

00:31:43.133 --> 00:31:44.635
your blade didn't make the cut.

00:31:44.702 --> 00:31:46.370
I'm going to have to ask you
to step off the forge floor.

00:31:46.437 --> 00:31:47.538
Thank you very much.

00:31:47.605 --> 00:31:49.140
Congratulations.

00:31:49.240 --> 00:31:50.841
Well, I'm going to have
to find a different way

00:31:50.908 --> 00:31:52.109
to take my wife
to go see Bigfoot,

00:31:52.176 --> 00:31:53.544
but we're still going to go.

00:31:56.480 --> 00:31:58.750
Well, Gunnar, that makes you
the "Forged in Fire" champion.

00:31:58.816 --> 00:32:01.619
You just got yourself
a check for $10,000.

00:32:01.686 --> 00:32:02.620
Congratulations.

00:32:02.687 --> 00:32:03.621
Thank you.

00:32:03.721 --> 00:32:05.823
Appreciate it, guys.

00:32:05.923 --> 00:32:08.226
I just won "Forged in Fire."

00:32:08.293 --> 00:32:09.560
Feeling good?

00:32:09.660 --> 00:32:11.229
I mean, I never
thought I would

00:32:11.295 --> 00:32:13.264
make it this far from day one.

00:32:13.331 --> 00:32:15.900
I don't necessarily think
that I'm a better smith

00:32:15.966 --> 00:32:17.101
than any of these other guys.

00:32:17.201 --> 00:32:19.270
It just worked out
in my favor today.

00:32:19.337 --> 00:32:22.173
As far as the money, after
football season ends,

00:32:22.239 --> 00:32:25.609
my wife and I will probably
take a long weekend somewhere.

00:32:25.710 --> 00:32:29.414
[music playing]

